      "reasoning": "The user wants me to make a Russian billiards (pool) game. This is a fun creative task. Let me think about what \"русский бильярд\" (Russian billiards) is.\n\nRussian billiards (русский бильярд) is a specific variant of pool played on a table with 6 pockets, using 16 balls: 15 numbered balls (1-15) plus a cue ball. The balls are:\n- 1 (yellow) - \"шар\"\n- 2 (blue)\n- 3 (red)\n- 4 (purple)\n- 5 (orange)\n- 6 (green)\n- 7 (maroon/brown)\n- 8 (black)\n- 9-15 (striped versions of 1-7 colors)\n\nActually, in Russian billiards, the balls are:\n- 1-7: solid colors\n- 9-15: striped (the 8 is black, no 8-stripe)\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Russian billiards uses 16 balls:\n- 1 (yellow)\n- 2 (blue)\n- 3 (red)\n- 4 (purple)\n- 5 (orange)\n- 6 (green)\n- 7 (brown/maroon)\n- 8 (black)\n- 9 (yellow stripe)\n- 10 (blue stripe)\n- 11 (red stripe)\n- 12 (purple stripe)\n- 13 (orange stripe)\n- 14 (green stripe)\n- 15 (brown stripe)\n\nThe rules of Russian billiards:\n- Players must call the pocket\n- The cue ball must hit the lowest-numbered ball of the player's group first\n- If you pocket your ball, you continue\n- If you pocket the cue ball, it's a foul\n- The game is won by pocketing all your balls then the black (8)\n\nThis is a complex game to implement. Let me think about the scope. The user just said \"сделай игру русский бильярд\" (make a Russian billiards game). \n\nI should make a playable HTML/JS game. Given the complexity, I'll make a solid implementation with:\n- A billiards table with 6 pockets\n- 16 balls (15 numbered + cue ball)\n- Physics (ball movement, collisions, friction)\n- Aiming and shooting mechanics\n- Basic rules\n\nLet me think about how much to implement. A full Russian billiards rules engine is quite complex. I'll make a good playable version with:\n- Physics simulation\n- Aiming with power control\n- Ball-ball collisions\n- Ball-pocket detection\n- Basic turn-based play (2 players or player vs simple AI)\n- Scoring\n\nLet me focus